Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 02:27:03 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Match transition tasks by task name, and stop guessing
 assignments

The audit matched a transition's action against the hook names. Those are different
values: the action is what a user clicks ('Register'), while the task the transition
carries names the hook ('Register Correspondence'). The comparison therefore found
nothing and reported a fully configured workflow as unconfigured.

Read each transition's task rows instead, report every task whose name resolves to no
hook, and flag hooks that are declared but attached to no transition.

Drop the automatic attach: which transition should run which lifecycle method is a
business decision that cannot be derived from metadata. Attach takes the three names
explicitly.
---
 murasalat_office/setup/workflow_tasks.py      | 199 ++++++++++++------
 .../tests/test_verification_contracts.py      |  19 +-
 2 files changed, 155 insertions(+), 63 deletions(-)

